{
    "background_story": "Marleigh was a skilled woodworker and furniture maker who spent most of her days in her cozy workshop. Her worktable, a sturdy oak behemoth, was the center of her creative universe. It was where she brought her designs to life, carefully crafting each piece with precision and love. Marleigh's worktable had been passed down to her from her grandfather, a master carpenter who had taught her the trade. Over the years, the table had accumulated scars, scratches, and stories, each one telling a tale of a project well-made. Marleigh cherished the worktable not just for its functionality, but for the memories and emotions it held. As she worked, she felt a deep connection to her grandfather and the generations of craftsmen who had worked on the same table before her.",
